  "proof_logic": {
    "ambient_inertia": "A compact fourteen-wall H9 chamber needs Gram inertia (9,1,4); a principal block with negative index two is impossible by Cauchy interlacing.",
    "compact_vertex_condition": "Every actual rank-nine vertex diagram must be elliptic.",
    "cross_edge_exhaustion": "No cross edge gives two orthogonal negative directions. At least two non-right cross edges fail an actual-vertex test, as do all labels m=4,5 in the one-edge case.",
    "minimal_nonface_condition": "All nine displayed missing five-faces must simultaneously support labelled order-five Lanner diagrams.",
    "one_edge_residue": "The 1,932 locally surviving m=3 representative trials split into four rooted block classes. The two large classes, of total size 1,860, have exact principal-block inertia (8,2,0).",
    "simultaneous_lanner_csp": "The remaining 72 representative trials admit zero mutually consistent choices from the complete 420-placement tables on the other seven missing five-faces.",
    "symmetry_coverage": "Four independent clone transpositions preserve the complete selected nerve and reduce each 420-state Lanner support to 110 representatives; their actions on the two supports factor, so both placements can be normalized simultaneously."
  },
